Create a production-ready Next.js application architecture and configure Cursor project rules.

Requirements:

1. Create a Cursor rules file:
.cursor/rules/project-rules.mdc

The rules should enforce:

- Next.js App Router
- TypeScript only
- Tailwind CSS only
- Cloudinary for image management
- Reusable component architecture
- Strong typing
- No usage of "any"
- JSDoc comments on every component, function, custom hook, and complex logic
- Conventional file and folder naming
- Conventional Git commits
- Clean scalable architecture

2. Create this folder structure:

src/
├── app/
│   ├── admin/
│   ├── api/
│   ├── layout.tsx
│   └── page.tsx
│
├── components/
│   ├── ui/
│   ├── common/
│   ├── forms/
│   └── layouts/
│
├── features/
├── hooks/
├── services/
├── lib/
├── types/
├── utils/
└── constants/

3. Add README.md containing:

- Project architecture explanation
- Development guidelines
- Naming conventions
- Component creation rules
- Git commit conventions
- How to add new features

4. Add example reusable components:

components/ui/
- button.tsx
- input.tsx
- modal.tsx
- loader.tsx

Each component must:
- Use TypeScript props
- Use Tailwind CSS
- Include JSDoc documentation
- Be reusable

5. Add example hooks:

hooks/
- use-auth.ts
- use-fetch.ts

Each hook must:
- Have proper TypeScript typing
- Include JSDoc comments

6. Add Cloudinary service structure:

services/
- cloudinary-service.ts

Include typed functions:

- uploadImage()
- deleteImage()
- getImageUrl()

with proper documentation.

7. Add admin portal structure:

src/app/admin/

Create:

- layout.tsx
- page.tsx
- dashboard components folder

Include:
- Admin sidebar component
- Dashboard card component
- Responsive layout

8. Configure the project with best practices:

- ESLint
- Prettier
- TypeScript strict mode
- Tailwind configuration
- Import aliases (@/)

9. Follow these coding rules:

- Components use PascalCase
- Files use kebab-case
- Hooks start with "use"
- Functions use camelCase
- Constants use UPPER_CASE
- No duplicate components
- Search existing code before creating new files

10. After creating everything:
- Explain the architecture
- Explain how to use Cursor rules
- Provide the first conventional commit message

Do not generate unnecessary code. Create only clean production-ready structure.